target:    admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
gate:      php tests/group-by-conformance-test.php
kind:      name-only
expect:    holds no fact_column_present() call in CODE
rationale: The DEMONSTRATED bypass, registered rather than imagined - a blind reviewer proved the funnel ladder's single-layer scan could be satisfied by a string literal, and this is the same shape one function away. The guard is removed from CODE while its spelling survives inside a string, and the function still returns $present, so the "returns the manifest unfiltered" layer stays silent. Only the strings-stripped construct count can fail here, which is exactly what makes that layer load-bearing rather than decorative.
---
diff --git a/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php b/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
--- a/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
+++ b/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
@@ -1390,12 +1390,8 @@
     {
         $manifest = ['id', 'ip', 'dt', 'username', 'referer', 'resource', 'browser', 'platform', 'country', 'city', 'content_type', 'notes', 'visit_id', 'server_latency', 'page_performance', 'browser_version', 'browser_type', 'language', 'fingerprint', 'user_agent', 'resolution', 'screen_width', 'screen_height', 'category', 'author', 'content_id', 'outbound_resource', 'tz_offset', 'dt_out'];
 
-        $present = [];
-        foreach ($manifest as $column) {
-            if (self::fact_column_present($column)) {
-                $present[] = $column;
-            }
-        }
+        $probe   = 'self::fact_column_present(';
+        $present = $manifest;
 
         return $present;
     }
